  partName: Oil Pan
  description: The Oil Pan, positioned at the middle-center-center of the Hover Engine,
    is a large and complex-shaped component that stores the engine's lubricating
    oil and provides a reservoir for the oil pump. Its standard surface material
    and design enable efficient oil flow and heat management. Interestingly, the
    Oil Pan's design must balance oil capacity and flow rates with engine performance,
    fuel efficiency, and emissions considerations to ensure optimal engine operation.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
